b03re6aud03"}, {"type": "text", "content": "She was a very  "}], "type": "question"}, {"contents": {"type": "", "content": "person."}, "type": "post_question"}, {"type": "objective", "content": "secondary_8"}]}], "type": "TYP", "id": 10, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": " \nErica talks about her old neighbor.\n"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Instructions: Listen to the audio. Type in the missing word. "}], "type": "post_instructions"}]}, {"template_override": 1, "stimuli_ids": [], "questions": [{"responses": [{"correct": 0, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 0, "selected": 0}, {"correct": 1, "_data": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "id": 1, "selected": 0}], "id": 0, "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}], "type": "question"}]}], "type": "RSLT", "id": 11, "_data": [{"contents": [], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Quiz"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": ""}, {"type": "text", "content": ""}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2, "incorrect_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "Whoops! Something important is missing."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Maybe next time..."}]}}]}], "type": "scholar", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "has_nav", "content": true}, {"type": "has_exercise_controls", "content": true}], "type": "lab_options"}], "id": 0, "stimuli": [{"type": "welcome", "template_override": 1, "_data": [], "id": 0, "contents": [{}]}, {"contents": [{"type": "slideshow", "value": {"coverimg": "engenn6le06ob03re2img02.jpg", "audiosrc": "engenn6le06ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "engenn6le06ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"time": "100", "image": "engenn6le06ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "Surreal ... eccentric ... imaginative ... These three words capture the essence of Salvador Dali, a prominent Spanish painter. I'm sure you have seen his most famous work, called <span class=\"italic\">The Persistence of Memory</span>, completed in 1931. Dali's life was as offbeat as his work."}, {"time": "22000", "image": "engenn6le06ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "He worked passionately  with other art forms, including photography, film and sculpture and worked with other artists of the time. He loved oriental clothes, luxurious goods and indulged excessively in everything . Dali's behavior was often described as grandiose and attention-grabbing, often more so than his artwork. His used both classical and modernist styles in his work and many of his critics enjoyed his \u201cstrange\u201d creations."}, {"time": "52800", "image": "engenn6le06ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 3, "text": "He was born in 1904 in Spain. He traveled to Paris and eventually his work was shown in London and then in the United States. He lived there after World War II and then returned to Spain where he and his wife stayed until his death in 1968."}]}}], "template_override": 1, "title": "", "type": "audio", "id": 1, "_data": []}]}], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Famous Artists"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "The Artist's Life"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "scholar > Grammar - part 1 > Superstars Today"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 6}, {"type": "level", "content": "B1.1"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Accurately use important information about people's jobs and places of work in communicative situations."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_3", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_4", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_5", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_6", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_7", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}, {"type": "secondary_8", "content": "Understands important and some specific information and aspects of attitude and intention using a range of appropriate language, in written or spoken documents or presentations."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to talk about a famous artist."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "   Describing Personality and Behavior"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use adjectives and adverbs to describe a person's personality and behavior."}, {"type": "text", "content": "You describe personality when you say how a person usually is. It is true most of the time. You use the verb to be + adjectives. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "You describe behavior when you say what a person does or how a person is at a particular time. You use the verb to be + adjectives or expressions like <span class=\"italic\">you were acting ... </span>or <span class=\"italic\">you behaved</span> + adverb."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":2,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\" Describing Personality \\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Describing Behavior\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"grandiose<br> attention-grabbing <br>offbeat <br>strange<br> eccentric <br>imaginative\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"He was ... yesterday <br>I/you/he behaved ... + adverb\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Dali was an eccentric person. (personality) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Dali indulged excessively in everything. (behavior)"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "surreal "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "very strange; unusual; bizarre "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali's paintings are surreal."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "eccentric "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "uncommon; not normal "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali was an eccentric person. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": " imaginative"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " full of new and interesting ideas "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali's paintings are imaginative."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to capture"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " to express accurately in words "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The word imaginative captures the idea of Dali's paintings."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "essence "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "spirit; the main idea of something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Surreal describes the essence of Dali's work."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "passionately"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "with passion"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adverb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": " Example: Dali worked passionately with other art forms."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "luxurious"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "expensive and elegant   "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali loved luxurious things."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud07"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "oriental "}, {"type": "definition", "content": " Asian; from Eastern Asia "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali loved oriental clothes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud08"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grandiose"}, {"type": "definition", "content": " impressive; over-the-top "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": " (adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali enjoyed a grandiose lifestyle"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud09"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "excessive "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "more than is normal or necessary "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(adjective)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Dali's behavior was excessive. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn6le06ob03aud10"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "engenn6le06ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "The Present Perfect vs The Simple Past Tense "}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the Present Perfect and the Past Simple  for events that started or happened in the past.  The difference is that the <span class=\"strong\">Simple Past</span> is used for   past events that happened at a very specific time,  while actions with no specific time are expressed in the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>.<br/>  You can also use the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>  when the past finished action has  a connection with the present. Observe the set of examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">I saw The Persistence of Memory at the  museum one month ago.<br/> Action Painting has been one of the most visited attractions.<br/> Art has changed my life.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "   There are regular verbs in the  <span class=\"Strong\">Simple Past</span>.  You add <span class=\"italic\">-ed</span>  to the basic form of the verb to conjugate them.<br/><br/> <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>: <br/><span class=\"italic\">I visited the Louvre museum 5 years ago.<br/> He painted many masterpieces when he was young.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": " In the <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>,  you use the auxliliary verb <span class=\"strong\">have</span> or  <span class=\"strong\">has</span>.  The name of the tense is  <span class=\"strong\">Present Perfect</span>  because the conjugation of the auxiliary verb follows the rules of the Simple Present form. Let's remember:"}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>:<br/>  <span class=\"italic\">I  <span class=\"strong\">paint</span> portraits.  I <span class=\"strong\">have painted</span> more than 50 portraits.<br/> She <span class=\"strong\">paints</span> portraits.   She <span class=\"strong\">has painted</span> more than 50 portraits.</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Apart from the auxiliary verb  <span class=\"strong\">have</span>/<span class=\"strong\">has</span>,  you need the principal verb or action in the  <span class=\"strong\">past participle</span> form.  <br/>Some verbs can be regular verbs. Their conjugation is  exactly the same to the Simple Past form, that is, you add <span class=\"strong\">- ed</span>. "}, {"type": "text", "content": " <span class=\"strong\">Examples</span>:<br/> <span class=\"italic\">Has art <span class=\"strong\">influenced</span> you?<br/> Dali's paintings <span class=\"strong\">have inspired</span> me.<br/> I <span class=\"strong\">have learned</span> a lot about Dali.</span>"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Cut a piece of paper into \u215b pieces."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On four pieces, write 4 verbs in the Simple Present tense."}, {"type": "text", "content": "On the other four pieces, write 4 adjectives or adverbs."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With a partner, mix up the pieces, choose one and then use that word to start a brief conversation. For example: The word \u201cgo\u201d - Have you gone to a museum? Where was it? What did you see? etc."}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I write down words to use in a conversation."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I start a conversation with a word."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I continue the conversation by asking follow-up questions."}]}]}